{
  "case_id": "2001-00-952",
  "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Maureen M. Flanagan (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FLANAGAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it\nplease the Court:\nIn 1988, Congress enacted the spousal\nimpoverishment protections of the Federal Medicaid Act, 42\nU.S. Code section 1396r-5, to accomplish two competing\npurposes. First, Congress sought to protect spouses\nliving at home from impoverishment when the other spouse\nis institutionalized and requires long-term nursing home\ncare. Secondly, Congress sought to ensure that married\ncouples seeking medicaid bear a fair share of the cost of\nsuch care."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, and let me ask you a question\non this point, if I may. There is a section, 5(b)(1), r-\n5(b)(1) of section 1396 that says that pre-eligibility,\nnone of the income of the community spouse shall be deemed\navailable to the institutionalized spouse, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Ms. Flanagan, it might help if -- I\nthink one of the main features of this legislation was\nthat income from the community spouse was never to be\nattributed to the institutionalized spouse, but vice\nversa, there is no such prohibition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey A. Lamken (United States, amicus)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LAMKEN: Yes, Your Honor. It's our --\nQUESTION: Now, are there proposed regulations\nof HHS that would allow either resource-first or income-\nfirst rules?\nMR. LAMKEN: Yes, Your Honor. There's currently\na pending rulemaking before HHS, and the Secretary in the\nnotice of proposed rulemaking has determined that States\nshould be permitted to decide whether to use the income-\nfirst methodology or the resource-first --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey A. Lamken (United States, amicus)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LAMKEN: Justice Scalia, I think the answer\ncomes in two parts. The first is, one doesn't have to\nthink that the statute means two different things at once\nin order to accept the Secretary's view. Community\nspouse's income can have a meaning, but there may be\ndifferent methodologies, all of which are reasonable, for\ndetermining and calculating what is the community spouse's\nincome."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Mitchell Hagopian)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HAGOPIAN: We don't exactly know. According, I believe, to the petition, the State estimated that it's in the neighborhood of 30 to 35 States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Have you read the notice of the proposed rulemaking?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Do we owe any deference to the agency here in its interpretation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-952",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "501d248b407b9fbaca04c776085a2026562d78ddfd3a2d08ba76ea802f74f15f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-501d248b407b-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
